Backport IDN host canonicalisation fix for GHSA-4c8g-83qw-93j6 (CVE-2026-13676).

Use WHATWG URL hostname parsing instead of the non-existent URL.domainToASCII
helper so Unicode/IDN hosts are canonicalised to their ASCII form before
host-policy checks. URL.domainToASCII is not a real API and threw, leaving the
raw Unicode host in place; attackers could smuggle look-alike / full-width
characters past host allow-list checks.

Ref: https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/security/advisories/GHSA-4c8g-83qw-93j6

The upstream regression test (test/security.test.js) is not shipped in the
3.0.6 target tree, so a replacement test written in the target's tape idiom is
added here.

